{"ts":"2026-08-20T20:11:18.429Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"0c521f6b9de253ca0feab1e1","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-c90tfh","claim:pm-ob9z4y","release:pm-rggtvd"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-c90tfh+pm-ob9z4y","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-c90tfh","claim:pm-ob9z4y","release:pm-rggtvd"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Context\nThe existing blocking assertion counts all blocks rows identically. The live population was exactly at its ceiling, while accepted graph reconstruction requires adding ordering edges backed by recorded evidence.\n\n## Decision\nRetain total blocks as a diagnostic measurement. Define evidence-cited blocks by the explicit evidence: source-kind prefix. Define uncited blocks as total minus evidence-cited. Move the existing anti-fabrication ceiling to the uncited population and add a floor over evidence-cited rows. Both remain blocking and carry adjacent pass/fail negative controls.\n\n## Consequences\nAdding an evidence-cited ordering edge cannot spend anti-fabrication headroom. Deleting recovered ordering fails the evidence floor. Adding a block without the evidence prefix fails the uncited ceiling. Changing either population still requires a verified Decision."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-jhpby4"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"ADR: Ordering assurance partitions evidence-cited blocks from uncited blocks"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Authorize the blocks ratchet to preserve its anti-fabrication ceiling over non-evidence rows while separately flooring evidence-cited ordering."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Decision"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-20T20:11:18.429Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-20T20:11:18.429Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The existing blocks ceiling is retargeted to total blocks minus evidence-cited blocks; Evidence-cited blocks receive an independent non-regression floor; Both assertions carry executable boundary negative controls and remain blocking in graph-composition"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"Provable history"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Keep anti-fabrication and recovered ordering simultaneously enforceable"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Evidence-backed historical ordering can grow without weakening graph governance"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Unblocks pm-c90tfh and its three ordering-lineage dependents"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Provenance-partitioned blocking assertions replace one contradictory global count"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The live global blocks ceiling is exactly saturated and rejected the required evidence-backed edges"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-m2u1"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-4jqm","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-20T20:11:18.429Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"evidence:pm-c90tfh","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-c90tfh","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-20T20:11:18.429Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"evidence:pm-c90tfh","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-dwj33e","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-20T20:11:18.429Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"evidence:pm-c90tfh","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at